  "worked_solution": "The third-degree Taylor polynomial approximation is\n\n$$\n{P}_{3}(x)=-5-7(x-4)-5(x-4)^{2}-\\frac{13}{6}(x-4)^{3}.\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(3.9)$ by evaluating the third-degree Taylor polynomial approximation at $x=3.9.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.9) & ≈{P}_{3}(3.9) \\\\  & =-5-7(3.9-4)-5(3.9-4)^{2}-\\frac{13}{6}(3.9-4)^{3} \\\\  & =-5-7(-0.1)-5(-0.1)^{2}-\\frac{13}{6}(-0.1)^{3} \\\\  & ≈-4.348.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
